  Size (--size): 8.0 GiB  [given]
      up to 280.0 GiB allowed on /
  Existing swap (--existing): replace  [given]
      keep      total swap 16.0 GiB: /swap.img stays, the new one is added with priority 10 and used first
    * replace   total swap 8.0 GiB: /swap.img — swapoff and commented out in /etc/fstab; the file stays on disk (to delete: --delete-old)
  Old swap files (--delete-old): keep  [default — flag not given]
    * keep      /swap.img (8.0 GiB) stays on disk: rollback can restore it
      delete    frees 8.0 GiB; rollback recreates empty swap files of the same size

Profile: zswap-lz4 — experimental: not confirmed by an SSD benchmark

Parameters
  PARAMETER         NOW     NEW       CURRENT SOURCE
  zswap.enabled     N    →  Y         kernel default
  zswap.compressor  lzo  →  lz4       kernel default
  zswap.zpool       —       zsmalloc  not in this kernel — skipped
  unchanged: zswap.max_pool_percent=20, vm.swappiness=60, vm.page-cluster=3, vm.watermark_scale_factor=10, vm.vfs_cache_pressure=100

Checks
  [ok]   root: running as root
  [info] path: /ramplus.swapfile (default)
  [ok]   filesystem: ext4 on /dev/fake_ (mount point /): swapfile via fallocate
  [ok]   disk: NVMe (nvme)
  [info] existing swap: /swap.img (file, 8.0 GiB, used 0 B, priority -2): --existing=replace selected
  [info] priority: the new swap gets priority 10 (above the existing swap (-2): the new one is used first)
  [ok]   space: / has 300.0 GiB of 500.0 GiB available; after creation 292.0 GiB would remain, at least 20.0 GiB is required (10% of the disk, but no more than 20.0 GiB and no less than 5.0 GiB)
  [ok]   memory for swapoff /swap.img: /swap.img is not in use — swapoff is safe
  [warn] status: experimental profile: not confirmed by scripts/bench.sh on a real SSD — applied only with explicit confirmation (in scripts: --experimental)
  [info] zswap.zpool: this kernel has no zpool parameter: zsmalloc is used — skipped
  [info] original values: first profile apply: the current system values are saved to /var/lib/ramplus/state.json for ramplus profile reset

Steps
   1. create /ramplus.swapfile, 8.0 GiB (fallocate; if the filesystem cannot — write zeros), mode 600
   2. chmod 600 /ramplus.swapfile
   3. mkswap /ramplus.swapfile
   4. swapon /ramplus.swapfile (priority 10)
   5. write /etc/systemd/system/ramplus.swapfile.swap
   6. systemctl daemon-reload
   7. systemctl enable ramplus.swapfile.swap
   8. swapoff /swap.img
   9. comment out line "/swap.img\tnone\tswap\tsw\t0\t0" in /etc/fstab (backup in /var/lib/ramplus/backups)
  10. systemctl daemon-reload
  11. zswap.compressor = lz4 (write to /sys/module/zswap/parameters/compressor)
  12. zswap.enabled = Y (write to /sys/module/zswap/parameters/enabled)
  13. write /etc/sysctl.d/99-ramplus.conf
  14. write /etc/systemd/system/ramplus-zswap.service
  15. systemctl daemon-reload
  16. systemctl enable ramplus-zswap.service
  (content of files to be written: --verbose)

Summary
  swap: 8.0 GiB → 8.0 GiB
  profile: zswap-lz4
  created: /etc/sysctl.d/99-ramplus.conf, /etc/systemd/system/ramplus-zswap.service, /etc/systemd/system/ramplus.swapfile.swap, /ramplus.swapfile
  disabled: /swap.img, fstab line «/swap.img none swap sw 0 0»
  deleted: —

Result: the plan can be applied. Apply: sudo ramplus setup --size 8G --existing=replace --profile zswap-lz4   (experimental profile: confirmation or --experimental will be required)

